# `.privacy-markers` — your own names, handles and hostnames.
#
# This file is git-ignored on purpose: `scripts/check-privacy.mjs` reads it,
# but the list itself never reaches the public repository. Without it the
# scanner still checks credentials, e-mail addresses and home paths.
#
# One entry per line, `#` starts a comment:
#
#   keyword       matched with word boundaries, case-insensitive — handles,
#                 short names, initials. e.g. `jdoe`
#   *substring    matched anywhere, case-insensitive — hostnames, account ids,
#                 anything that appears glued to other text. e.g. `*my-laptop`
#
# Add your GitHub handle, your real name, your machine's hostname and any
# private project prefix you use. Then run: npm run check:privacy -- --verbose
